<figure id="S0.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26847v1/images/example.png" id="S0.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:467/709;" width="467" height="709" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Example of a tokenized representation (using GPT-4o) of an English text (top) and a ciphered version of it using Caesar Cipher (bottom).
While both containing the same number of characters (613), the original version is constructed of 128 tokens, while the ciphered version
is constructed of 294 tokens — more than double.</figcaption>
</figure>
